<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Mesopotamia and Iran</p><h1 class="st-title">Der</h1><p class="st-meta">2000 BCE – 1750 BCE (approx.) · capital Der</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A frontier city between Mesopotamia and Elam, guarding the road to the Iranian highlands and sacred to the god Ishtaran.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Der, modern Tell Aqar near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/badra-iraq">Badra</a>, lay at the foot of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagros-mountains">Zagros</a> on the main route from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tigris">Tigris</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/susa">Susa</a>. It was a city from the third millennium BCE and a province of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/neo-sumerian-empire">Neo-Sumerian Empire</a>. After Ur collapsed around 2000 BCE, local rulers governed it independently.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Der was a small buffer state whose position made it valuable to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elam">Elam</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/eshnunna">Eshnunna</a> and the cities of the south. Its patron god <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ishtaran">Ishtaran</a>, a judge deity represented by a serpent, was worshipped in the temple E-dimgalkalama. A local king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anum-muttabbil">Anum-muttabbil</a>, claimed in an inscription to have smitten Elam, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-anshan">Anshan</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/shimashki-dynasty">Shimashki</a>, the clearest sign of the city's independent ambitions. Otherwise its rulers are poorly known.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Der lost its independence in the 18th century BCE, falling to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/eshnunna">Eshnunna</a> and then to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hammurabi">Hammurabi's</a> <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/babylonian-empire">Babylonian Empire</a>. It remained an important border fortress: in 720 BCE the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-der">Battle of Der</a> was fought there between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sargon-ii">Sargon II</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/assyrian-empire">Assyrian Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elamites">Elamites</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 2000 BCE – 1750 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">city state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Mesopotamia and Iran</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:19.90%;width:4.98%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>2000 BCE – 1750 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/21st-century-bce">21st century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century-bce">18th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Der</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Anum-muttabbil</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Mesopotamian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Akkadian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/iraq">Iraq</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Durum, Tell Aqar</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-1875&amp;focus=der" aria-label="Der on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5856 975 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Der lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6176 1231L6193 1305M6176 1231L6143 1252"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6193 1305h0M6143 1252h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6176 1231h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6176 1231h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Der. <a href="/atlas?year=-1875&amp;focus=der">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
